{"name":"Purple Hyacinth","hex":"#6e8fc0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"},{"term":"hyacinth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any bulbous plant of the genus Hyacinthus, native to the Mediterranean and South Africa.","A variety of zircon, ranging in color from brown, orange, reddish-brown and yellow; a jacinth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hyacinth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hyacinth","blocks":[{"text":"Hyacinthus is a genus of bulbous herbs and spring-blooming perennials. They are fragrant flowering plants in the family Asparagaceae, subfamily Scilloideae and are commonly called hyacinths. The genus is native predominantly to the Eastern Mediterranean region from the south of Turkey to the Palestine region, although naturalized more widely."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Hyacinth_-_Anglesey_Abbey.jpg/330px-Hyacinth_-_Anglesey_Abbey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyacinth"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Hyacinthus_transcaspicus_GotBot_2015.JPG/500px-Hyacinthus_transcaspicus_GotBot_2015.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Hyacinthus_transcaspicus_GotBot_2015.JPG/1280px-Hyacinthus_transcaspicus_GotBot_2015.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Hyacinthus_transcaspicus_GotBot_2015.JPG/500px-Hyacinthus_transcaspicus_GotBot_2015.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hyacinthus transcaspicus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHyacinthus_transcaspicus_GotBot_2015.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Nowruz_Sonbol_%28Hyacinth%29.JPG/500px-Nowruz_Sonbol_%28Hyacinth%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Nowruz_Sonbol_%28Hyacinth%29.JPG/500px-Nowruz_Sonbol_%28Hyacinth%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nowruz Sonbol (Hyacinth)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANowruz_Sonbol_(Hyacinth).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/P1130470_Hyacinthus_orientalis_Common_hyacinth_%28Hyacinthaceae%29.JPG/120px-P1130470_Hyacinthus_orientalis_Common_hyacinth_%28Hyacinthaceae%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&